        {
          "id": 410170235,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I just did\n\n    git push -o ci.skip scratchpad +HEAD\n\n(my \"fork\" of Wireshark isn't any meaningful flavor of \"downstream\", it's just a scratchpad required for the GitLab review process).  I'm still seeing the spinning pipeline status.\n\nShould I try just closing this one and creating a new one?\n\n(And is there any flavor of \"close this and permanently erase it from GitLab's memory\", so that it doesn't show up as a merge request any more, ever, and isn't reopenable?)",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
